===Pronunciation===
* {{enPR|grēv}}, {{IPA|en|/ɡɹiːv/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-grieve.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{homophones|en|grieve}}
* {{rhymes|en|iːv|s=1}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|en|enm|greve}}, from {{inh|en|ang|grǣfe}}, {{m|ang|græfe|grǣfa|bush, bramble, grove, thicket, copse, brush-wood (for burning), fuel}}, probably related to {{der|en|gem-pro|*grōbō|t=ditch, hole}}.

Cognate with {{cog|sco|greve}}, {{m|sco|greave|t=grove}}. Compare also {{cog|gem-pro|*grainiz||twig}}, of unknown origin, whence {{cog|non|grein||branch, bough}}. Closely related to {{cog|ang|grāf}}, {{m|ang|grāfa||grove}}. See {{l|en|grove}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|obsolete}} A [[bush]]; a [[tree]]; a [[grove]].
#* {{RQ:Spenser Faerie Queene|6|2|passage=she fled into that covert '''greave'''}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} A [[bough]]; a [[branch]].

===Etymology 2===
From {{inh|en|enm|greve}}, {{m|enm|greyve}}, from {{inh|en|ang|grǣfa}}, {{m|ang|grēfa||pit, cave, hole, grave, trench}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*grōbō||pit, ditch}} {{rfv-etym|en}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*gʰrebʰ-||to dig, scratch, scrape}}. Cognate with {{cog|frr|groop||pit, sewer, gutter}}, {{cog|nl|groef||pit, hole, gutter}}, {{cog|de|Grube||pit, hole}}, {{cog|is|gröf||pit, grave}}. Possible {{doublet|en|groove|nocap=1}}; also related to {{m|en|grave}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|obsolete}} A [[ditch]] or [[trench]].

===Etymology 3===
From {{inh|en|enm|greve}}, {{m|enm|grayve}}, from {{der|en|fro|greve||shin}}, of uncertain origin; possibly from {{cog|arz|جورب||stocking, leg cover}}.<ref>Klein, Dr. Ernest, A Comprehensive Etymological Dictionary of the English Language, Amsterdam: Elsevier Scientific Publishing Co., 1971.</ref> Watkins suggests a connection with {{m|fro|greve|t=part in the hair}}, due to the resemblance of the medial ridge to a part in the hair, from {{m|fro|graver|t=to part (the hair); engrave}}, of {{der|en|gem|-}} origin, from {{der|en|frk|*graban|t=to engrave}};<ref>{{R:American Heritage Dictionary|greave}}</ref> if so, related to Etymology 2 above.

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# A piece of [[armour]] that protects the [[leg]], especially the [[shin]], and occasionally the [[top]]s of the [[feet]].
#* {{seeCites|en}}

